            0.89,
            0.798
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Grade 8 You may recall learning earlier that a force can make an Curiosity object move from rest, change the speed and direction Chapter 5 of motion of a moving object, and can even change the shape of an object. For example, a ball at rest starts moving when you apply a force, a force applied by a cricket bat on a cricket ball changes its direction, and a lemon can be squeezed by the force applied by your fingers (Fig. 6.1)."
            }
          ]
        },
